{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordPositionTracking"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.allOdd_posAfter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.allOdd_posAfter","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L166-L169","doc":"…and all runs odd: one class, and the permutation is the upward shift on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.allEven_posAfter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.allEven_posAfter","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L157-L164","doc":"**Not vacuous, and it exercises both branches.** All runs even: every class is a\nsingleton and the permutation is the identity on each — `π i = pStart e i = i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.step_within_class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.step_within_class","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L144-L155","doc":"**The class is traversed upward.** Consecutive strands in the same class are joined by\nan odd run, and the closure permutation sends one to the next — so a class is connected\ninside a single cycle.\n\nTogether with `compIdx_posAfter` (cycle ⊆ class) this gives **cycles = classes**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lt_compIdx_of_lt_pStart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lt_compIdx_of_lt_pStart","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L122-L142","doc":"**`pStart e i` is the least element of `i`'s class**: everything strictly below it\nsits in a strictly earlier class.\n\nWith `compIdx_pStart` (same class) this pins `pStart e i` as the class minimum, which is\nwhat makes `posAfter_of_even` close the cycle rather than merely stay inside it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.pStart_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.pStart_le","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L113-L120","doc":"`pStart e i` never exceeds `i` — it is the left end of a walk that only moves down. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.compIdx_posAfter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.compIdx_posAfter","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L101-L111","doc":"**The closure permutation preserves the class.** Both branches land in `compIdx e i`:\nthe odd one because an odd run contributes nothing to the count, the even one by\n`compIdx_pStart`.\n\nHence every cycle of the closure lies inside a single `compIdx` class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.posAfter_of_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.posAfter_of_even","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L93-L99","doc":"**An even run wraps `i` back to `pStart e i`.** Runs above `i` leave it alone and run\n`i` does not move it, so the closure permutation returns the strand that was sitting at\nposition `i` when run `R_i` began — which `posAfter_self` identifies as `pStart e i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.posAfter_of_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.posAfter_of_odd","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L85-L91","doc":"**An odd run fuses `i` with `i+1`.** The closure permutation sends `i` to `i + 1`:\nruns above `i` cannot touch it (`posAfter_stab`), run `i` swaps it up, and runs below\ncannot reach `i+1` (`posAfter_of_le`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.posAfter_stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MonotoneWordCycleStructure.posAfter_stab","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MonotoneWordCycleStructure.lean#L65-L83","doc":"**Runs above `j` leave `j` alone.** Run `g` moves only positions `g` and `g+1`, so a\nposition strictly below `g` is untouched — the other half of `posAfter_of_le`, which\nhandled positions strictly above. ","signatureChunk":0}]}